        <mxCell id="AbJ37FA1o0RB3voxti96-23" edge="1" parent="x-8thJ_eOBKoUWWDrhoA-1" source="AbJ37FA1o0RB3voxti96-14" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;" target="AbJ37FA1o0RB3voxti96-15" value="">
          <mxGeometry height="50" relative="1" width="50" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="300" y="360" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="350" y="310" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="AbJ37FA1o0RB3voxti96-24" parent="x-8thJ_eOBKoUWWDrhoA-1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;aspect=fixed;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" value="&lt;h2&gt;Video Streaming — Quick Interview Notes&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot; role=&quot;heading&quot;&gt;Key Video Streaming Terminology&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;overflow-wrap: break-word; margin: 16px 0px;&quot;&gt;Before diving into how the service works, here are the foundational terms you need to know:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;Transcoding:&lt;/span&gt; The process of converting a video file from one format, size, or bitrate to another (e.g., converting a massive &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;background-color: rgb(244, 246, 247); border: 1px solid rgb(244, 246, 247); border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px;&quot;&gt;.mov&lt;/code&gt; file from a camera into a compressed &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;background-color: rgb(244, 246, 247); border: 1px solid rgb(244, 246, 247); border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px;&quot;&gt;.mp4&lt;/code&gt; web video).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;Bitrate:&lt;/span&gt; The amount of data processed per second of video, usually measured in Megabits per second (Mbps). Higher bitrates mean better quality but larger file sizes and slower loading times.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;HLS (HTTP Live Streaming):&lt;/span&gt; An adaptive video streaming protocol developed by Apple. Instead of playing one giant file, it splits the video into tiny pieces and delivers them dynamically based on the viewer&#39;s internet speed.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;Segments (Chunks):&lt;/span&gt; The tiny, individual video files (usually 2 to 10 seconds long, ending in &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;background-color: rgb(244, 246, 247); border: 1px solid rgb(244, 246, 247); border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px;&quot;&gt;.ts&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;background-color: rgb(244, 246, 247); border: 1px solid rgb(244, 246, 247); border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px;&quot;&gt;.m4s&lt;/code&gt;) that make up an HLS stream.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;Manifest File (&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;background-color: rgb(244, 246, 247); border: 1px solid rgb(244, 246, 247); border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px;&quot;&gt;.m3u8&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; A text-based playlist file that acts as an index or map. The video player reads this file to know exactly which video chunks to download and play next.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;Adaptive Bitrate Streaming (ABR):&lt;/span&gt; The technology that automatically switches video quality (e.g., dropping from 1080p to 480p) mid-stream if a user’s internet connection slows down, preventing the video from buffering.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;hr style=&quot;height: 1px; border-width: 1px 0px 0px; border-style: solid none none; border-color: rgb(220, 223, 229) currentcolor currentcolor; border-image: none;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot; role=&quot;heading&quot;&gt;What AWS Elemental MediaConvert Does: Step-by-Step&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;overflow-wrap: break-word; margin: 16px 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;AWS Elemental MediaConvert&lt;/span&gt; is a serverless, file-based video processing engine. When you feed it a raw video file from Amazon S3, it automatically executes the following six steps:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;background-color: rgb(244, 246, 247); padding: 16px; display: flex; gap: 16px; overflow-x: auto;&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;pre style=&quot;margin: 0; overflow: auto hidden&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-unset&quot;&gt;[ Raw Video ] ➔ [1. Ingest &amp;amp; Analyze] ➔ [2. Decode] ➔ [3. Scale &amp;amp; Encode] ➔ [4. Slice Chunks] ➔ [5. Write Manifests] ➔ [6. Save to S3]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot; role=&quot;heading&quot;&gt;1. Ingestion &amp;amp; Analysis&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;overflow-wrap: break-word; margin: 16px 0px;&quot;&gt;MediaConvert securely connects to your &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;S3 Input Bucket&lt;/span&gt; and fetches the source video. It scans the file to read its blueprint, identifying its original resolution, frame rate, audio tracks, and color settings.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot; role=&quot;heading&quot;&gt;2. Decoding &amp;amp; Cleaning&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;overflow-wrap: break-word; margin: 16px 0px;&quot;&gt;It unpacks the compressed video into raw, uncompressed frames. During this stage, it applies automatic filters to clean up the video if needed—such as fixing interlaced lines from older cameras or adjusting frame rates.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot; role=&quot;heading&quot;&gt;3. Multi-Resolution Transcoding&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;overflow-wrap: break-word; margin: 16px 0px;&quot;&gt;This is the core processing phase. MediaConvert duplicates the raw video frames and compresses them into multiple resolutions and bitrates simultaneously (e.g., &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;1080p&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;720p&lt;/span&gt;, and &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;480p&lt;/span&gt;) based on your settings.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;overflow-wrap: break-word; margin: 16px 0px;&quot;&gt;💡 &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;Smart Savings (QVBR):&lt;/span&gt; MediaConvert uses built-in AI called &lt;em style=&quot;font-weight: inherit;&quot;&gt;Quality-Defined Variable Bitrate&lt;/em&gt;. If a scene is simple (like a person talking against a plain background), it automatically lowers the bitrate to save you storage and bandwidth costs. It only spikes the bitrate during fast-moving action scenes where detail is needed.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot; role=&quot;heading&quot;&gt;4. Chunk Segmentation&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;overflow-wrap: break-word; margin: 16px 0px;&quot;&gt;Once the multiple resolutions are created, MediaConvert slices them into exact, bite-sized &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;6-second segments&lt;/span&gt;. It precisely aligns the starting point of each chunk across all resolutions. This ensures that if a player switches a user from 720p to 1080p, the transition happens instantly without a visual stutter.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot; role=&quot;heading&quot;&gt;5. Manifest Compilation&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;overflow-wrap: break-word; margin: 16px 0px;&quot;&gt;As it creates the chunks, it automatically writes the text-based map files:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;Variant Manifests:&lt;/span&gt; It creates a playlist for each resolution (e.g., &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;background-color: rgb(244, 246, 247); border: 1px solid rgb(244, 246, 247); border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px;&quot;&gt;video_1080p.m3u8&lt;/code&gt;), listing all its specific 6-second chunks in chronological order.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;Master Manifest:&lt;/span&gt; It creates one overarching file (&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;background-color: rgb(244, 246, 247); border: 1px solid rgb(244, 246, 247); border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px;&quot;&gt;master.m3u8&lt;/code&gt;) that links all the variant playlists together. This is the main link you give to your video player.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot; role=&quot;heading&quot;&gt;6. Secure Delivery to S3&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;overflow-wrap: break-word; margin: 16px 0px;&quot;&gt;Finally, MediaConvert saves the entire package—the master manifest, the individual resolution manifests, and the hundreds of tiny segment chunks—straight into your &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;S3 Output Bucket&lt;/span&gt;. Once the last file is uploaded, it fires a success signal and shuts down, costing you nothing until your next video upload.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;overflow-wrap: break-word; margin: 16px 0px;&quot;&gt;Would you like to explore how to set up &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;security controls&lt;/span&gt; on your S3 output bucket so that &lt;em style=&quot;font-weight: inherit;&quot;&gt;only&lt;/em&gt; your authorized website or application can play these video chunks?&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;overflow-wrap: break-word; margin: 16px 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;overflow-wrap: break-word; margin: 16px 0px;&quot;&gt;articles to use multipart&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;overflow-wrap: break-word; margin: 16px 0px;&quot;&gt;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sdk-for-javascript/v3/developer-guide/emc-examples-jobs.html&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;overflow-wrap: break-word; margin: 16px 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="1750" width="1750" x="30" y="680" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="AbJ37FA1o0RB3voxti96-25" edge="1" parent="x-8thJ_eOBKoUWWDrhoA-1" source="AbJ37FA1o0RB3voxti96-0" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;exitX=1;exitY=0.25;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.667;entryY=1;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;entryPerimeter=0;" target="AbJ37FA1o0RB3voxti96-3" value="">
          <mxGeometry height="50" relative="1" width="50" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="400" y="350" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="450" y="300" as="targetPoint" />
